# 📍 Flask Location Detection Demo

A simple Flask-based web application that demonstrates how a browser can request **user-approved geolocation**, send the coordinates to a Python backend, and convert the coordinates into a **readable approximate address** using reverse geocoding.

> **Privacy:** This project only accesses browser location after the user explicitly grants location permission. It is intended for learning and authorized demonstrations.

---

## 🚀 Features

- 🌐 Flask web application
- 📍 Browser Geolocation API
- 🔐 User permission-based location access
- 📡 Sends latitude and longitude to Flask
- 🗺️ Reverse geocoding using OpenStreetMap Nominatim
- 📋 Displays latitude and longitude
- 📌 Displays the approximate readable address
- ⚡ Simple HTML frontend
- 🐍 Python backend

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Backend programming |
| Flask | Web server |
| HTML | Frontend |
